\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Empirical pretraining objective}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{pretraining}
\tag{loss}

\p{For a finite training multiset #{S=(x^{(1)},\ldots,x^{(N)})}, the
\newvocab{empirical pretraining objective} is
##{
\widehat L_S(\theta)
=\frac1N\sum_{i=1}^{N}\ell(\theta;x^{(i)}).
}}

\p{The training setup in \citet{sec. 2.2}{kaplan2020scaling} reports loss on
finite sampled data. The empirical objective depends on the realized corpus,
its multiplicities, and its weighting. It need not equal the population
objective in \ref{ftip-000Z}.}
